WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.049 --> 00:00:05.800
On May 30th 1938, accountant Carl Wilkes married
Crysilda Berryman in Bakersfield, CA.

00:00:05.800 --> 00:00:10.600
Just one year later, they gave birth to their
son, Paul Emery Wilkes, but on April 1st 1943,

00:00:10.600 --> 00:00:14.660
they would return to the Bakersfield Receiving
Hospital, this time to deliver a daughter.

00:00:14.660 --> 00:00:16.730
But this was no April Fools joke.

00:00:16.730 --> 00:00:20.480
Annie Wilkes is main antagonist of Stephen
King’s Misery, a character he created to

00:00:20.480 --> 00:00:22.900
represent his fear of his most obsessive fans.

00:00:22.900 --> 00:00:27.260
But Annie’s history goes much deeper than
what we see in the film adaptation of Misery,

00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:31.339
so stick around to the end of this video to
see me analyse her entire life’s story,

00:00:31.339 --> 00:00:34.980
including how she planned to take revenge
on Paul after escaping the house.

